<title>USA: Carter-Wallace stake lifted by Gabelli.</title>
<headline>Carter-Wallace stake lifted by Gabelli.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by New York investment manager Mario Gabelli said Tuesday it raised its stake in Carter-Wallace Inc to 2,617,500 common shares or 7.70 percent from 6.56 percent previously held.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include a net 229,500 common shares bought between January 23 to March 7 at prices $13.125 to $16.50 per share.</p>
<p>Carter-Wallace, based in New York, manufactures and sells personal hygiene products, such as antiperspirants and deodorants.</p>
</text>
